   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **Franklin's Tower** (1 review): Features beautiful guitar work from John [9]\n- **Estimated Prophet** (1 review): Played in a reggae style, which the reviewer loves [4]\n- **A Love Supreme** (1 review): Reviewer notes something happening just before the band moves into this piece (text cut off) [3]\n- **St. Stephen** (1 review): Mayer's playing here sounds like something from his John Mayer Trio work [5]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Man Smart, Woman Smarter**: rare: 10 archived performances [11]\n- **A Love Supreme**: rare: 4 archived performances [11]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2017-11-14.travitz.schoepsMK4v.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 19 songs; 179 min; rated 4.5/5 by 6 [1]. Said about its sound: Mix is the main flaw: Mayer's guitar overpowers the rest of the band [4]\n- **deadco2017-11-14**: source not stated; 19 songs; 179 min; rated 4.5/5 by 2 [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Reviewer attended nine shows and rates this the best of them by far [3]\n- Reviewer's favorite Dead and Company show; considers it a milestone for Mayer's guitar playing [4]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2017-11-14.travitz.schoepsMK4v.flac16**: taped by Jeff Travitz; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps MK4V's>KCY>VMS5u>SD744t [1]. Also: Schoeps MK4V mics into KCY preamp and VMS02ib, recorded on Sound Devices 744t from back of GA pit; Transferred via Sound Forge Pro 11 for fades, CDWAV tracking, Trader's Little Helper to FLAC, Foobar2000 tagging [1]\n- **deadco2017-11-14**: taped by Richie Stankiewicz; transferred by Richie Stankiewicz; source: FOB, Sweet Spot [2]",
